  {
   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "L12_006_Where To Insert",
   "display_name": "Where To Insert",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A useful variant of binary search finds <b>where a value belongs</b> in a sorted list: the first index whose item is <b>greater than or equal to</b> <code>x</code> (or <code>len(L)</code> if every item is smaller). Inserting <code>x</code> there keeps the list sorted. This version never stops early, so it always takes about <code>log n</code> looks:</p>\n<pre>insert_position(L, x):\n    lo = 0\n    hi = len(L)\n    while lo &lt; hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if probe(L, mid) &lt; x:\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return lo</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>insert_position(L, x)</code> following the pseudocode exactly, for a list <code>L</code> sorted from small to large.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>insert_position([10, 20, 30, 40], 25)</code> returns <code>2</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# ---- Helper functions: do not change them; the tests count how often you call them ----\ndef probe(L, i):\n    # Look at the item at index i. Use this EVERY time you read an item.\n    return L[i]\n\n\ndef insert_position(L, x):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(insert_position([10, 20, 30, 40], 25))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"probe\": 0}\n_probe = probe\ndef probe(*args):\n    _c[\"probe\"] += 1\n    return _probe(*args)\nprint(insert_position([10, 20, 30, 40], 25), 'looks:', _c['probe'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2 looks: 2",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"probe\": 0}\n_probe = probe\ndef probe(*args):\n    _c[\"probe\"] += 1\n    return _probe(*args)\nprint(insert_position([10, 20, 30, 40], 5), insert_position([10, 20, 30, 40], 99))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0 4",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
