  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "L12_007_Bubble Sort",
   "display_name": "Bubble Sort",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>Sorting</b> puts a list in order. <b>Bubble sort</b> is the simplest method: walk through the list comparing <b>neighbours</b>; whenever a pair is in the wrong order, swap it. After one pass, the biggest item has \"bubbled up\" to the end. Repeat, each pass one item shorter:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">start:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">8</td></tr></table><table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">after pass 1:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">8</td></tr></table><table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">after pass 2:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">8</td></tr></table><table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">after pass 3:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">8</td></tr></table><table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">after pass 4:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">8</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">blue: the part that is already in its final place (the biggest items 'bubble' to the end)</div>\n<pre>bubble_sort(L):\n    n = len(L)\n    for i = 0, 1, ..., n - 2:              # passes\n        for j = 0, 1, ..., n - 2 - i:      # neighbours (j, j + 1) not yet in place\n            if greater(L, j, j + 1):\n                swap(L, j, j + 1)</pre>\n<p>Use the helpers <code>greater(L, i, j)</code> (is <code>L[i] &gt; L[j]</code>?) and <code>swap(L, i, j)</code>. The tests count both. The number of comparisons is always <code>n * (n - 1) / 2</code>: bubble sort is <b>O(n²)</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>bubble_sort(L)</code> following the pseudocode exactly. It sorts <code>L</code> in place (small to large) and returns nothing.</p>\n<p>For example, sorting <code>[5, 1, 4, 2, 8]</code> takes 10 comparisons and 4 swaps.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# ---- Helper functions: do not change them; the tests count how often you call them ----\ndef greater(L, i, j):\n    # True if the item at index i is bigger than the item at index j.\n    return L[i] > L[j]\n\n\ndef swap(L, i, j):\n    # Exchange the items at indexes i and j.\n    L[i], L[j] = L[j], L[i]\n\n\ndef bubble_sort(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [5, 1, 4, 2, 8]\n# bubble_sort(L)\n# print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"greater\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_greater = greater\ndef greater(*args):\n    _c[\"greater\"] += 1\n    return _greater(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [5, 1, 4, 2, 8]\nbubble_sort(L)\nprint(L, 'comparisons:', _c['greater'], 'swaps:', _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 4, 5, 8] comparisons: 10 swaps: 4",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
