   "xml_index": 8,
   "xml_name": "L12_008_Bubble Sort With Early Stop",
   "display_name": "Bubble Sort With Early Stop",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>If a whole pass makes <b>no swaps</b>, the list is already sorted, and we can stop. With this change, an already sorted list needs only <b>one</b> pass (<code>n - 1</code> comparisons, <b>O(n)</b>: the <b>best case</b>), while a reversed list still needs all passes (<b>O(n²)</b>: the <b>worst case</b>).</p>\n<pre>bubble_sort_early(L):\n    n = len(L)\n    for i = 0, 1, ..., n - 2:\n        swapped = False\n        for j = 0, 1, ..., n - 2 - i:\n            if greater(L, j, j + 1):\n                swap(L, j, j + 1)\n                swapped = True\n        if not swapped:\n            stop (return)</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>bubble_sort_early(L)</code> following the pseudocode exactly.</p>\n<p>For example, for the already sorted list <code>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</code> it makes 4 comparisons and 0 swaps.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# ---- Helper functions: do not change them; the tests count how often you call them ----\ndef greater(L, i, j):\n    # True if the item at index i is bigger than the item at index j.\n    return L[i] > L[j]\n\n\ndef swap(L, i, j):\n    # Exchange the items at indexes i and j.\n    L[i], L[j] = L[j], L[i]\n\n\ndef bubble_sort_early(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n# bubble_sort_early(L)\n# print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
