  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L12_013_Partition",
   "display_name": "Partition",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>Quicksort</b> is a fast sorting method built on <b>partitioning</b>: choose one item as the <b>pivot</b> (here: the <b>last</b> item of the part), then rearrange the part so that all items <b>smaller</b> than the pivot come first, then the pivot, then the rest. After partitioning, the pivot is in its <b>final</b> sorted place.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">before:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">7</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">9</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">the pivot is the last item, 5</div>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">after:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(57,136,195);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">9</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">smaller items first, then the pivot at index 3, then the bigger ones</div>\n<pre>partition(L, lo, hi):          # rearrange L[lo..hi]; the pivot is L[hi]\n    i = lo                     # next place for a smaller item\n    for j = lo, lo + 1, ..., hi - 1:\n        if less(L, j, hi):     # L[j] &lt; pivot\n            swap(L, i, j)\n            i = i + 1\n    swap(L, i, hi)             # put the pivot in its place\n    return i</pre>\n<p>Follow the pseudocode exactly (it swaps even when <code>i</code> equals <code>j</code>; that is fine and is counted).</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>partition(L, lo, hi)</code> following the pseudocode exactly. It rearranges the part <code>L[lo]</code> to <code>L[hi]</code> (with <code>lo &lt;= hi</code>) and returns the final index of the pivot.</p>\n<p>For example, for <code>L = [7, 2, 9, 4, 1, 5]</code>, <code>partition(L, 0, 5)</code> returns <code>3</code> and <code>L</code> becomes <code>[2, 4, 1, 5, 9, 7]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# ---- Helper functions: do not change them; the tests count how often you call them ----\ndef less(L, i, j):\n    # True if the item at index i is smaller than the item at index j.\n    return L[i] < L[j]\n\n\ndef swap(L, i, j):\n    # Exchange the items at indexes i and j.\n    L[i], L[j] = L[j], L[i]\n\n\ndef partition(L, lo, hi):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [7, 2, 9, 4, 1, 5]\n# print(partition(L, 0, 5), L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [7, 2, 9, 4, 1, 5]\np = partition(L, 0, 5)\nprint(p, L, 'comparisons:', _c['less'], 'swaps:', _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3 [2, 4, 1, 5, 9, 7] comparisons: 5 swaps: 4",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [9, 1, 5, 3, 7]\np = partition(L, 1, 3)\nprint(p, L, _c['less'], _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2 [9, 1, 3, 5, 7] 2 2",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [4]\nprint(partition(L, 0, 0), L, _c['less'], _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0 [4] 0 1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = list(map(int, input().split()))\np = partition(L, 0, len(L) - 1)\nprint(p, L, _c['less'], _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "3 8 1 9 2 6 5",
     "expected": "3 [3, 1, 2, 5, 8, 6, 9] 6 4",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [1, 2, 3, 4]\nprint(partition(L, 0, 3), L, _c['less'], _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3 [1, 2, 3, 4] 3 4",
