  {
   "xml_index": 14,
   "xml_name": "L12_014_Quicksort",
   "display_name": "Quicksort",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>Quicksort</b> sorts a part <code>L[lo..hi]</code> <b>recursively</b> (Lab 5!):</p>\n<ol><li>if the part has fewer than 2 items (<code>lo &gt;= hi</code>), it is already sorted (<b>base case</b>);</li><li>otherwise <b>partition</b> it; the pivot lands at index <code>p</code>;</li><li>quicksort the part left of the pivot, <code>L[lo..p-1]</code>, and the part right of it, <code>L[p+1..hi]</code>.</li></ol>\n<pre>quicksort(L, lo, hi):\n    if lo &lt; hi:\n        p = partition(L, lo, hi)\n        quicksort(L, lo, p - 1)\n        quicksort(L, p + 1, hi)</pre>\n<p>To sort a whole list: <code>quicksort(L, 0, len(L) - 1)</code>.</p>\n<p>When the pivots split the parts roughly in half, there are about <code>log n</code> levels of splitting, each doing about <code>n</code> comparisons in total: <b>O(n log n)</b>, much faster than O(n²) for big lists. (With an unlucky pivot every time, for example on an already sorted list with the last item as pivot, it degrades to O(n²).)</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the function <code>partition</code> from the previous question is given. Write the recursive function <code>quicksort(L, lo, hi)</code> following the pseudocode exactly.</p>\n<p>For example, sorting <code>[7, 2, 9, 4, 1, 5]</code> takes 9 comparisons and 7 swaps.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# ---- Helper functions: do not change them; the tests count how often you call them ----\ndef less(L, i, j):\n    # True if the item at index i is smaller than the item at index j.\n    return L[i] < L[j]\n\n\ndef swap(L, i, j):\n    # Exchange the items at indexes i and j.\n    L[i], L[j] = L[j], L[i]\n\n\ndef partition(L, lo, hi):\n    i = lo\n    for j in range(lo, hi):\n        if less(L, j, hi):\n            swap(L, i, j)\n            i = i + 1\n    swap(L, i, hi)\n    return i\n\n\ndef quicksort(L, lo, hi):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [7, 2, 9, 4, 1, 5]\n# quicksort(L, 0, len(L) - 1)\n# print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [7, 2, 9, 4, 1, 5]\nquicksort(L, 0, len(L) - 1)\nprint(L, 'comparisons:', _c['less'], 'swaps:', _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 9] comparisons: 9 swaps: 7",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = []\nquicksort(L, 0, -1)\nprint(L, _c['less'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[] 0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]\nquicksort(L, 0, 7)\nprint(L, 'comparisons:', _c['less'])",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8] comparisons: 28",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = list(map(int, input().split()))\nquicksort(L, 0, len(L) - 1)\nprint(L, _c['less'], _c['swap'])",
     "stdin": "5 3 8 1 9 2 7",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 9] 11 10",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "_c = {\"less\": 0, \"swap\": 0}\n_less = less\ndef less(*args):\n    _c[\"less\"] += 1\n    return _less(*args)\n_swap = swap\ndef swap(*args):\n    _c[\"swap\"] += 1\n    return _swap(*args)\nL = [3, 3, 1, 2, 3]\nquicksort(L, 0, 4)\nprint(L, _c['less'], _c['swap'])",
